assets/diagrams/vipi-dataset.svg:
How images get into the VIPI dataset
Download the dataset at the commit pinned in dataset.json with research.download; no account is needed. On the workbench Dataset page or with research.curation, add images with label, content type, source, license and provenance (duplicates are skipped), then label and review them: classification, OCR reference and payload, keeping each content type at 50 percent benign. After hf auth login, submit only your changes as a pull request on Hugging Face. A maintainer reviews image, labels and source; merging accepts them. To use them in VIPI, a GitHub pull request updates the revision in dataset.json and research.download fetches it.
