assets/diagrams/vipi-evaluation.svg:
How an evaluation run works
An evaluation scans every image of the development split (450 images; the test split of 104 only once). For each image VIPI looks for an earlier run with the same image bytes: if OCR settings, code and packages match and the earlier detection had no error, OCR and detection are reused; if only the OCR part matches, the OCR is reused and detection runs again; otherwise the image is scanned from scratch. The run summary holds metrics, time, cost, host and models. It is compared with the saved baseline, and a complete run can be saved as the new baseline in research/baselines and committed. --dry-run shows how many images are reused; --no-reuse-ocr scans everything.
