assets/diagrams/vipi-modes.svg:
Local and cloud mode
Local mode: install vipi-scanner with the ocr and detector-local extras, run vipi setup with the OCR mode to download pinned models (Prompt Guard needs a Hugging Face token), then scan without API calls; OCR runs on the CPU, Clef-Flash and d1 on CUDA, Apple MPS or CPU, and images stay on the machine. Cloud mode: install vipi-scanner with the ocr extra, run vipi setup --modus cloud, which downloads nothing and costs nothing, set the provider API keys, then scan with --modus cloud; images go to the providers and each request is billed. Local and cloud cannot be mixed and there is no fallback.
